  <worksheets>
    <worksheet name='Where poverty sits'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontsize='13'>Where poverty sits</run><run fontsize='9'>  MICS 2021 · 5 bands, not 37 ranks · hover for MPI + 95% CI</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='Nigeria MPI polygons' name='federated.0mpipolygons' />
          </datasources>
          <datasource-dependencies>
      <column caption='state' datatype='string' name='[state]' role='dimension' type='nominal' semantic-role='[State].[Name]' />
      <column caption='pcode' datatype='string' name='[pcode]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
      <column caption='ring' datatype='integer' name='[ring]' role='dimension' type='ordinal' />
      <column caption='point_order' datatype='integer' name='[point_order]' role='dimension' type='ordinal' />
      <column caption='lon' datatype='real' name='[lon]' role='measure' type='quantitative' semantic-role='[Geographical].[Longitude]' />
      <column caption='lat' datatype='real' name='[lat]' role='measure' type='quantitative' semantic-role='[Geographical].[Latitude]' />
      <column caption='MPI band (Multidimensional Poverty Index)' datatype='string' name='[mpi_band]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
      <column caption='poverty_group' datatype='string' name='[poverty_group]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
      <column caption='mpi' datatype='real' name='[mpi]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='mpi_se' datatype='real' name='[mpi_se]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='mpi_ci_lo' datatype='real' name='[mpi_ci_lo]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='mpi_ci_hi' datatype='real' name='[mpi_ci_hi]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='headcount_ratio_pct' datatype='real' name='[headcount_ratio_pct]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='intensity_pct' datatype='real' name='[intensity_pct]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='mpi_poor_thousands' datatype='real' name='[mpi_poor_thousands]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='mpi_pct' datatype='real' name='[mpi_pct]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='mpi_ci_lo_pct' datatype='real' name='[mpi_ci_lo_pct]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='mpi_ci_hi_pct' datatype='real' name='[mpi_ci_hi_pct]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='gov_party' datatype='string' name='[gov_party]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
      <column caption='dim_hover' datatype='string' name='[dim_hover]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
      <column-instance column='[lat]' derivation='Avg' name='[avg:lat:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
      <column-instance column='[lon]' derivation='Avg' name='[avg:lon:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
      <column-instance column='[state]' derivation='None' name='[none:state:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
      <column-instance column='[pcode]' derivation='None' name='[none:pcode:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
      <column-instance column='[ring]' derivation='None' name='[none:ring:ok]' pivot='key' type='ordinal' />
      <column-instance column='[point_order]' derivation='None' name='[none:point_order:ok]' pivot='key' type='ordinal' />
      <column-instance column='[mpi_band]' derivation='None' name='[none:mpi_band:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
      <column-instance column='[headcount_ratio_pct]' derivation='Sum' name='[sum:headcount_ratio_pct:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
      <column-instance column='[intensity_pct]' derivation='Sum' name='[sum:intensity_pct:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
      <column-instance column='[mpi_poor_thousands]' derivation='Sum' name='[sum:mpi_poor_thousands:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
      <column-instance column='[poverty_group]' derivation='None' name='[none:poverty_group:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
      <column-instance column='[mpi_pct]' derivation='Sum' name='[sum:mpi_pct:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
      <column-instance column='[mpi_ci_lo_pct]' derivation='Sum' name='[sum:mpi_ci_lo_pct:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
      <column-instance column='[mpi_ci_hi_pct]' derivation='Sum' name='[sum:mpi_ci_hi_pct:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
      <column-instance column='[gov_party]' derivation='None' name='[none:gov_party:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
      <column-instance column='[dim_hover]' derivation='None' name='[none:dim_hover:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
          </datasource-dependencies>
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style>
          <style-rule element='mark'><format attr='has-stroke' value='true' /><format attr='stroke-color' value='#FFFFFF' /><format attr='stroke-size' value='3' /></style-rule>
        </style>
      <panes>
        <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-allow'>
          <view>
            <breakdown value='auto' />
          </view>
          <mark class='Polygon' />
          <encodings>
            <lod column='[federated.0mpipolygons].[none:state:nk]' />
            <lod column='[federated.0mpipolygons].[none:pcode:nk]' />
            <lod column='[federated.0mpipolygons].[none:ring:ok]' />
            <path column='[federated.0mpipolygons].[none:point_order:ok]' />
            <color column='[federated.0mpipolygons].[none:mpi_band:nk]' />
            <text column='[federated.0mpipolygons].[none:state:nk]' />
            <lod column='[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:headcount_ratio_pct:qk]' />
            <lod column='[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:intensity_pct:qk]' />
            <lod column='[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:mpi_poor_thousands:qk]' />
            <lod column='[federated.0mpipolygons].[none:poverty_group:nk]' />
            <lod column='[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:mpi_pct:qk]' />
            <lod column='[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:mpi_ci_lo_pct:qk]' />
            <lod column='[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:mpi_ci_hi_pct:qk]' />
            <lod column='[federated.0mpipolygons].[none:gov_party:nk]' />
          </encodings>
          <customized-tooltip show-buttons='false'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontsize='13'><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[none:state:nk]>]]></run>
              <run> &#183; </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[none:poverty_group:nk]>]]></run>
              <run> of the 37 states, by MPI&#10;Of the population, </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:headcount_ratio_pct:qk]>]]></run>
              <run>% are multidimensionally poor&#10;</run>
              <run>Average deprivation among them: </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:intensity_pct:qk]>]]></run>
              <run>% of the things counted&#10;</run>
              <run>Poor people: </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:mpi_poor_thousands:qk]>]]></run>
              <run> thousand&#10;</run>
              <run>Made up of: </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[none:dim_hover:nk]>]]></run>
              <run>&#10;</run>
              <run>Governorship 1999&#8211;2021: </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[none:gov_party:nk]>]]></run>
              <run bold='true'>&#10;&#10;MPI </run>
              <run bold='true'><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:mpi_pct:qk]>]]></run>
              <run bold='true'>%</run>
              <run>  (95% interval </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:mpi_ci_lo_pct:qk]>]]></run>
              <run>% to </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpipolygons].[sum:mpi_ci_hi_pct:qk]>]]></run>
              <run>%)&#10;</run>
              <run italic='true'>MPI is the share of people who are poor multiplied by how deprived they are, as a percentage of the index.&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run italic='true'>Neighbouring states' intervals overlap, so the map groups states into bands instead of ranking them.</run>
            </formatted-text>
          </customized-tooltip>
          <style>
            <style-rule element='mark'>
              <format attr='mark-labels-show' value='true' />
            </style-rule>
          </style>
        </pane>
      </panes>
        <rows>[federated.0mpipolygons].[avg:lat:qk]</rows>
        <cols>[federated.0mpipolygons].[avg:lon:qk]</cols>
      </table>
    </worksheet>
    <worksheet name='Where poverty clusters'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontsize='13'>Where poverty clusters</run><run fontsize='9'>  Each state coloured by its own poverty and its neighbours' — descriptive, not a significance test</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='Spatial polygons' name='federated.0mpispatialpoly' />
          </datasources>
          <datasource-dependencies>
      <column caption='state' datatype='string' name='[state]' role='dimension' type='nominal' semantic-role='[State].[Name]' />
      <column caption='pcode' datatype='string' name='[pcode]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
      <column caption='ring' datatype='integer' name='[ring]' role='dimension' type='ordinal' />
      <column caption='point_order' datatype='integer' name='[point_order]' role='dimension' type='ordinal' />
      <column caption='lon' datatype='real' name='[lon]' role='measure' type='quantitative' semantic-role='[Geographical].[Longitude]' />
      <column caption='lat' datatype='real' name='[lat]' role='measure' type='quantitative' semantic-role='[Geographical].[Latitude]' />
      <column caption='mpi_band' datatype='string' name='[mpi_band]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
      <column caption='poverty_group' datatype='string' name='[poverty_group]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
      <column caption='mpi' datatype='real' name='[mpi]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='mpi_se' datatype='real' name='[mpi_se]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='mpi_ci_lo' datatype='real' name='[mpi_ci_lo]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='mpi_ci_hi' datatype='real' name='[mpi_ci_hi]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='headcount_ratio_pct' datatype='real' name='[headcount_ratio_pct]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='intensity_pct' datatype='real' name='[intensity_pct]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='mpi_poor_thousands' datatype='real' name='[mpi_poor_thousands]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='This state&apos;s poverty score (MPI, % of index)' datatype='real' name='[mpi_pct]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='mpi_ci_lo_pct' datatype='real' name='[mpi_ci_lo_pct]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='mpi_ci_hi_pct' datatype='real' name='[mpi_ci_hi_pct]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='gov_party' datatype='string' name='[gov_party]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
      <column caption='dim_hover' datatype='string' name='[dim_hover]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
      <column caption='Neighbourhood type (this state&apos;s poverty, beside the states it borders&apos;)' datatype='string' name='[spatial_group]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
      <column caption='Average poverty score of the states it borders (MPI, % of index)' datatype='real' name='[spatial_lag_mpi_pct]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column caption='Number of states it borders' datatype='integer' name='[neighbours]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
      <column-instance column='[lat]' derivation='Avg' name='[avg:lat:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
      <column-instance column='[lon]' derivation='Avg' name='[avg:lon:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
      <column-instance column='[state]' derivation='None' name='[none:state:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
      <column-instance column='[pcode]' derivation='None' name='[none:pcode:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
      <column-instance column='[ring]' derivation='None' name='[none:ring:ok]' pivot='key' type='ordinal' />
      <column-instance column='[point_order]' derivation='None' name='[none:point_order:ok]' pivot='key' type='ordinal' />
      <column-instance column='[spatial_group]' derivation='None' name='[none:spatial_group:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
      <column-instance column='[mpi_pct]' derivation='Sum' name='[sum:mpi_pct:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
      <column-instance column='[spatial_lag_mpi_pct]' derivation='Sum' name='[sum:spatial_lag_mpi_pct:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
      <column-instance column='[neighbours]' derivation='Sum' name='[sum:neighbours:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
      <column-instance column='[dim_hover]' derivation='None' name='[none:dim_hover:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
          </datasource-dependencies>
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style>
          <style-rule element='mark'><format attr='has-stroke' value='true' /><format attr='stroke-color' value='#FFFFFF' /><format attr='stroke-size' value='3' /></style-rule>
        </style>
      <panes>
        <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-allow'>
          <view>
            <breakdown value='auto' />
          </view>
          <mark class='Polygon' />
          <encodings>
            <lod column='[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[none:state:nk]' />
            <lod column='[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[none:pcode:nk]' />
            <lod column='[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[none:ring:ok]' />
            <path column='[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[none:point_order:ok]' />
            <color column='[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[none:spatial_group:nk]' />
            <text column='[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[none:state:nk]' />
            <lod column='[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[sum:mpi_pct:qk]' />
            <lod column='[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[sum:spatial_lag_mpi_pct:qk]' />
            <lod column='[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[sum:neighbours:qk]' />
          </encodings>
          <customized-tooltip show-buttons='false'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontsize='13'><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[none:state:nk]>]]></run>
              <run> &#183; </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[none:spatial_group:nk]>]]></run>
              <run>&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true'>Poverty score: </run>
              <run bold='true'><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[sum:mpi_pct:qk]>]]></run>
              <run bold='true'>%</run>
              <run>&#10;Made up of: </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[none:dim_hover:nk]>]]></run>
              <run>&#10;Average of the </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[sum:neighbours:qk]>]]></run>
              <run> states it borders: </run>
              <run><![CDATA[<[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[sum:spatial_lag_mpi_pct:qk]>]]></run>
              <run>%&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run italic='true'>The colour says two things at once. Grey is the poor block: this state is poorer than the average state, and so are the states it borders. Deep teal is the mirror image — better off than average, among better-off neighbours. Purple marks a state that does not fit its surroundings: poorer than average, with neighbours that are not. Read it as a description of where poverty sits, not as a list of places that stand out: the lines below give the one number that says how much of this is more than the north being poorer than the south.&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true'>The reading, in plain words&#10;</run>
              <run>Yes. States with similar poverty scores do tend to share a border. But most of that is simply that the north is poorer than the south: how far north a state sits explains about three quarters of what looks like neighbouring states resembling each other. Think of a height map. Two neighbours are usually at similar heights because the land slopes steadily — not because one hill lifts the next. Take the slope out, and only a little resemblance between neighbours is left. Only 1 of the 37 states stands out on its own, once we allow for having looked at 37 states at once.</run>
              <run>&#10;</run>
              <run italic='true'>Nothing here shows that one state's poverty affects its neighbour's — neighbours resembling each other is a fact about the map.&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true'>Technical details&#10;</run>
              <run>Moran's I of the poverty score 0.798 (p ≤ 0.0001, 9,999 shuffles); after accounting for how far north a state is, 0.244 (p = 0.0095); after latitude, conflict and climate together, 0.108 (p = 0.107). How far north a state is explains 77% of the pattern. 16 of 37 states look neighbourhood-like before correction; 1 (Yobe) stands out after correcting for 37 tests, and 0 with the stricter Benjamini–Yekutieli correction.</run>
            </formatted-text>
          </customized-tooltip>
          <style>
            <style-rule element='mark'>
              <format attr='mark-labels-show' value='true' />
            </style-rule>
          </style>
        </pane>
      </panes>
        <rows>[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[avg:lat:qk]</rows>
        <cols>[federated.0mpispatialpoly].[avg:lon:qk]</cols>
      </table>
    </worksheet>
    <worksheet name='How poverty is made up'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontsize='13'>How poverty is made up</run><run fontsize='9'>  each bar: one state's MPI split across OPHI's three areas · the split is exact, and the bar always totals 100% · shown by default: the five poorest states and the first twelve of the rest · add any other state from the state checklist card on the left rail · bars listed in MPI order, which is not a ranking · health is child mortality only (nutrition is excluded for every state), so it carries the full one-third weight</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='Poverty composition' name='federated.0mpidimshare' />
